we are duplicating code from an old sprawling tui + server implementation, into a new 'only server 'implementation.
    - old implementation has clanker.py entrypoint: all code obscured from view
        - this entrypoint and the code that it imports / uses has been hidden. 
    - new implementation has clank-server.py entrypoint: all code visible
        - uses code from the old system
        - all relevant code has also been copied over to content/backend dir
        - we are in process of updating imports, to make the new entrypoint rely on its own code only.
    - the two 'project' shall be disjointed in time.

so essentially we want to bring it to a state where the visible code does not depend upon 'invisible' code


 status:
 the entrypoint now only sources visible code.
 downstream from that - what remains?

